# FlowState release signing keys (SSH allowed-signers format, read by `git verify-tag`).
#
# `flowstate update` installs a release only if its git tag is signed by a key listed HERE,
# in the copy that is already installed (it reads this file before it changes anything; the
# list inside the new release is not trusted). An empty list means every update is refused
# with "no release signing key is set up yet".
#
# One line per key:   <principal> namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA... <comment>
# Public keys only. Never put a private key here. How to make the key and sign a release:
# docs/RELEASING.md.
#
# A new key must arrive in a release signed by a key that is already listed here.

flowstate-release namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIC5K/vdVxqPUXSmXW842s2NN2uJK7rpDj6/3bq39gmtq DialectForge FlowState release
